# Git and GitHub pushes

When the user asks to **push to git**, **push to GitHub**, or similar:

1. Run `git status` and `git diff` to review changes.
2. Stage relevant files (not `Productivity data/` — it is gitignored).
3. Commit using the **exact version title the user provides** as the commit message (e.g. `v0.2 Weekly chart tweaks`).
4. Push to `origin` on the current branch (`main` unless the user specifies otherwise).
5. Do not amend or force-push unless the user explicitly requests it.

If there are no changes to commit, say so and do not create an empty commit.
